Step 1: Update personService.js

Add a function to send a DELETE request.

import axios from "axios";

const baseUrl = "http://localhost:3001/persons";

const getAll = () => {
  return axios.get(baseUrl).then(response => response.data);
};

const create = (newPerson) => {
  return axios.post(baseUrl, newPerson).then(response => response.data);
};

const remove = (id) => {
  return axios.delete(`${baseUrl}/${id}`);
};

export default {
  getAll,
  create,
  remove
};

Notice we use the name remove instead of delete because delete is a reserved JavaScript keyword.

Step 2: Create the Delete Handler

In App.jsx, add:

const deletePerson = (id, name) => {
  const confirmDelete = window.confirm(`Delete ${name}?`);

  if (!confirmDelete) {
    return;
  }

  personService.remove(id).then(() => {
    setPersons(persons.filter(person => person.id !== id));
  });
};
What this does
Asks the user for confirmation.
Sends a DELETE request to the backend.
Removes the deleted person from React state.
React re-renders automatically.
Step 3: Add a Delete Button

If you're rendering your people like this:

{persons.map(person => (
  <p key={person.id}>
    {person.name} {person.number}
  </p>
))}

change it to:

{persons.map(person => (
  <p key={person.id}>
    {person.name} {person.number}
    <button onClick={() => deletePerson(person.id, person.name)}>
      delete
    </button>
  </p>
))}

The arrow function is important because you need to pass arguments to deletePerson.

What Happens?

Suppose you click delete for Ada Lovelace.

Step 1

The button runs:

deletePerson(2, "Ada Lovelace");
Step 2

React shows:

Delete Ada Lovelace?
Step 3

If you click OK:

personService.remove(2);

This sends:

DELETE http://localhost:3001/persons/2
Step 4

JSON Server deletes the record from db.json.

Step 5

After the request succeeds:

setPersons(persons.filter(person => person.id !== id));

If persons was:

[
  { id: 1, name: "Arto" },
  { id: 2, name: "Ada" },
  { id: 3, name: "Dan" }
]

After filtering:

[
  { id: 1, name: "Arto" },
  { id: 3, name: "Dan" }
]

React updates the UI automatically.

Final Flow
User clicks Delete
        │
        ▼
window.confirm()
        │
        ▼
User clicks OK
        │
        ▼
personService.remove(id)
        │
        ▼
HTTP DELETE /persons/:id
        │
        ▼
JSON Server removes the person
        │
        ▼
setPersons(persons.filter(...))
        │
        ▼
React re-renders without that person